/*! @brief Fiber operation object, this object cannot be created directly

 After creating a fiber using coroutine.start, this object is returned for fiber processing and inter-fiber communication.
 The fiber main function can access this fiber object through this, or get the current fiber through coroutine.current.
 ```JavaScript
 function func(v1)
 {
   console.log(v1 + this.v);
 }

 var fb = coroutine.start(func,100);

 fb.v = 123;

 fb.join();
 ```

 Fiber local storage is completed through the shared Fiber object, get the current fiber through coroutine.current, achieve the purpose of sharing data by modifying and querying its variables.

 ```JavaScript
 function func()
 {
   console.log(coroutine.current().v);
 }

 coroutine.current().v = 100;

 func();
 ```

 When a fiber is created, it will automatically copy the local variables of the current fiber to the new fiber, after that, modifications to each other's local variables will not affect each other, unless the variable itself is an object reference.

 ```JavaScript
 function func()
 {
   console.log(coroutine.current().v);
 }

 coroutine.current().v = 100;

 var fb = coroutine.start(func);

 coroutine.current().v = 200;

 fb.join();
 ```
 */
interface Fiber : object
{
    /*! @brief Wait for fiber to end */
    join();

    /*! @brief Query the unique id of the fiber */
    readonly Long id;

    /*! @brief Query the call stack of the fiber*/
    readonly String stack;

    /*! @brief Query the stack size used by the fiber*/
    readonly Integer stack_usage;
};